          "claim": "The map $R=2\\operatorname{id}_{X\\otimes X}$ is invertible. In the $\\mathbb C$-linear strictification used by [F1], the transported map is $2\\operatorname{id}$ on $X'\\otimes X'$. Hence both local operators on $X'^{\\otimes3}$ are $2\\operatorname{id}$, and each side of the Yang–Baxter equation is $8\\operatorname{id}$. Thus [F1] applies without identifying the tensor power with the original object $\\mathbb C$.",
