        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For scalars $\\lambda,\\mu\\in\\mathbb C$ and $f,h,g\\in V_{ab}^c$, linearity of composition gives $(\\lambda f+\\mu h)g^\\dagger=\\lambda fg^\\dagger+\\mu hg^\\dagger$, while conjugate-linearity of dagger gives $f(\\lambda g+\\mu h)^\\dagger=\\bar\\lambda fg^\\dagger+\\bar\\mu fh^\\dagger$. Taking the unique scalar coefficients from [F2] proves linearity in the first argument and conjugate-linearity in the second. Taking daggers of $fg^\\dagger=\\langle f,g\\rangle\\operatorname{id}_c$ gives $gf^\\dagger=\\overline{\\langle f,g\\rangle}\\operatorname{id}_c$, so $\\langle g,f\\rangle=\\overline{\\langle f,g\\rangle}$.",
